  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing towards Migration Governance in the Islamic Republic of Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human mobility in the Islamic Republic of Iran has been shaped by various factors over the past years - such as socio-economic fluxes and neighboring countries&apos; security situations, especially Afghanistan. Understanding and managing these complex movements is crucial for evidence-based policy making and implementation which are comprehensive and effective. While previous attention has been given to mobility between Iran and Afghanistan, as well as to Iran and Turkey, a need to focus on internal mobility dynamics and their positive impact on Iranian society and the economy is also recognized.To address this need, IOM Iran aims to conduct the first Migration Governance Indicators (MGIs) exercise for the country and establish a country-level United Nations Network for Migration (UNNM), along with capacity development specifically on the objectives of the Global Compact for Migration (GCM). To this end, the project&apos;s objective is to enhance migration governance in the Islamic Republic of Iran, empowering key government entities to address gaps in migration governance through awareness raised and knowledge gained from activities under this initiative. The project has one main outcome and three interrelated outputs. The outcome foresees for key national stakeholders to approve and utilize comprehensive and consistent migration indicators to assess Iran&#x2019;s migration governance framework, and engage in related dialogues through appropriate coordination structures. The achieve this outcome and feeds into the overall objective, the initiative will work towards  increasing awareness and understanding of migration governance tools and methodologies, such as the MGIs, across national stakeholders; build upon this awareness to conduct a thorough MGI process; and finally establish a country-level United Nations Network on Migration that informs the activities of the United Nations system in Iran with a focus on migration governance, to enhance migration-centered engagement between the UN, the government, and the international community more at large in Iran. This initiative will build on synergies with national stakeholders, intra-UN engagement in the country and dialogue between the UN system in Iran and the Government of Islamic Republic of Iran (GIRI), also in coordination with the UN Resident Coordinator Office (UNRCO).</narrative>
  </description>
